    "created_at": "2016-12-04T08:42:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-04T08:42:50Z",
    "body": "The `p` end tag is optional. I suppose `ref` is what is causing problems here. The `source` file is not actually HTML. I think a parse/serialize step could break things in subtle ways... For example if a `ref` element is used not as the last child, the rest of the text in that paragraph could disappear in the final output...\r\n\r\nWould it work to split with a more naïve approach and split the file with a regex for `<h2 filename=` or so, and then concat back together before passing it in to wattsi?",
